DEF("ka:law", S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:subset"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2))), A("ka:extra")), A("ka:allowed_extra"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:subset"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:dedup"), A("ka:differ")), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), A("ka:expected"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("ka:allowed_extra"))))))))),
"THE CONSTRAINT AGREEMENT LAW. Today`s base is alethically clean, so every violation the kernel answers over it must be accounted for: it is of a constraint whose span reaches a fact type in ka:expected, a population the kernel does not yet read in time, or of a constraint ka:findings names. MEASURED: V answers 36 violations over the base, all of the constraints ka:findings names for the values today`s reader files in text. It failed first with a uniqueness that took every row for a duplicate.",
DEF("ka:v_of", S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:dedup"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("k:V"), A("k:boot"))))),
