DEF("ka:mi_only", S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("k:alldecls")), A("ka:declared_names")))),
DEF("ka:acc_names", S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), A("ka:expected"), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("k:subtypefacts")), A("ka:mi_only")))))),
DEF("ka:unaccounted", S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ka:c_fts"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ka:c_fts"), N(1)), N(2)))))), K(PHI()), S2(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), A("ka:viol_cons"), A("ka:acc_names"))))), A("ka:findings")))),
"A violation is also accounted for when its constraint spans a subtype fact type (k:subtypefacts): their populations are the instance reflection, the kernel`s next part.",
"The kernel mints the 185 involvement links` readings with the Text and Predicate the metamodel makes mandatory, so ka:allowed_extra holds those 185 and 185 rows today lacks. FINDINGS, WHERE THE PAPER SAYS TODAY IS WRONG. V is over all of C_S (def:violation, thm:complete), and today`s base breaks two of its own mandatories, each for the 185 involvement links whose readings today`s reflection mints (rAPIIsInvolvedInAPIAcceptsObjectTypeAsParameter and the rest): Each Reading has some Text (MC:e:ReadingHasText#1) and each Reading is used by some Predicate (MC:e:ReadingIsUsedByPredicate#1). Today`s gate does not check them. The kernel`s own reflection mints those readings with their Text and Predicate, so neither finding is a violation of the kernel`s V, and ka:v_law again allows nothing unaccounted. And today`s reader files each value an instance sentence names, Position 1, 2 and 3 and Sequence Number 1 in the Constraint Span sentences, as an instance of its value type in text, where the roles that hold it hold it typed: so the instance-of fact of each such value is involved with two instances, the number and the text, which breaks the uniqueness of the four involvement links of instance-of and most-specifically-of in their second role, 32 violations, and each text value plays none of the roles its type`s disjunctive mandatory spans, 4 violations. Today`s gate checks neither. ka:findings names these constraints, and ka:v_law accounts for a violation of a constraint it names.",
DEF("ka:findings", K(S8(A("MC:e:ReadingHasText#1"), A("MC:e:ReadingIsUsedByPredicate#1"), A("UC:in:ObjectTypeInstanceIsInvolvedInObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType#2"), A("UC:in:ObjectTypeInstanceIsInvolvedInObjectTypeInstanceIsMostSpecificallyOfObjectType#2"), A("UC:in:ObjectTypeIsInvolvedInObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType#2"), A("UC:in:ObjectTypeIsInvolvedInObjectTypeInstanceIsMostSpecificallyOfObjectType#2"), A("DJ:i:ConstraintSpanHasPosition#2+ColumnHasPosition#2+PatternStepHasPosition#2+PatternStepReadsTheRoleInPosition#2+PositionIsInvolvedInRoleHasPositionInReading#1"), A("DJ:i:ConstraintSpanHasSequenceNumber#2")))),
DEF("ka:v_law", S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("ka:unaccounted")))
)
